WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:04.112
A long task is a chain of small successes.

00:04.288 --> 00:07.013
Miss one link, and it scores zero.

00:09.800 --> 00:12.294
Different tasks stall at different stages,

00:12.364 --> 00:14.781
so each needs its own diagnosis.

00:18.567 --> 00:22.506
We present ReFocus: Progress-Guided Adaptive Practice

00:22.536 --> 00:26.421
for Long-Horizon Robotic Manipulation Reinforcement Learning.

00:27.933 --> 00:29.731
The robot must fill a bowl,

00:29.815 --> 00:31.342
then store it in the fridge.

00:31.542 --> 00:34.075
First, it places the vegetable in the bowl.

00:34.375 --> 00:36.172
Next, it adds the chicken.

00:36.472 --> 00:38.142
Then it stalls at the fridge.

00:38.642 --> 00:42.632
Terminal reward: zero. Both completions ignored.

00:43.733 --> 00:45.158
Here is the pipeline.

00:45.258 --> 00:48.305
Global RL measures progress on the whole task.

00:48.405 --> 00:50.899
Local RL practices the bottleneck.

00:50.999 --> 00:53.738
Evaluation checks the whole task again.

00:55.233 --> 00:57.611
At its core is a task DAG.

00:58.611 --> 01:01.440
Every stage gets an equal share of reward.

01:02.040 --> 01:06.557
On MugInMicrowave, the success rate rises to 92 percent,

01:06.731 --> 01:09.701
from 68 percent with sparse rewards.

01:11.000 --> 01:15.916
Failed rollouts help too: the advantage rises where progress was made.

01:18.300 --> 01:20.639
Then ReFocus practices the stall,

01:20.787 --> 01:22.650
starting from the window entry.

01:22.750 --> 01:27.344
Normal, prefix, and suffix rollouts practice it in context.

01:29.433 --> 01:33.048
A history buffer records each window's cost and effect.

01:33.648 --> 01:39.121
After three rounds, ReFocus reaches 97.8 percent on LIBERO-Long

01:39.151 --> 01:43.500
and 51.3 percent on RoboCasa365.

01:45.100 --> 01:48.341
ReFocus outperforms other online RL methods,

01:48.476 --> 01:53.934
with the highest overall success rate on LIBERO-Long and RoboCasa365.

01:55.933 --> 01:58.350
Here is the success rate on each task,

01:58.614 --> 02:00.992
each evaluated over 50 episodes.

02:03.700 --> 02:06.439
On a Unitree G1 humanoid robot,

02:06.664 --> 02:09.531
we compare against SFT and RECAP.

02:09.731 --> 02:13.449
StackBowl: ReFocus reaches 100%,

02:13.662 --> 02:17.947
versus 80% for SFT and 90% for RECAP.

02:19.833 --> 02:26.541
On PickFruit, 100%, versus 75% and 85%.

02:28.833 --> 02:31.084
And on BreadBaker, the hardest,

02:31.114 --> 02:35.773
95%, versus 30% and 70%.

02:38.467 --> 02:41.515
We visualize the value model trained by RECAP:

02:41.598 --> 02:45.136
with ReFocus, its value is far steadier.

02:48.433 --> 02:49.986
Reward the progress.

02:50.186 --> 02:51.739
Practice the bottleneck.

02:51.939 --> 02:54.047
Practice, round by round.

02:57.047 --> 02:58.793
This, is ReFocus.
